# Credentials. freesound.key is the "Client secret/Api key" from the credential
# page and doubles as the OAuth2 client secret; the token file holds a live
# session. Neither belongs anywhere near a remote.
freesound.key
freesound-oauth.key
freesound-oauth-token.json

# index.html IS committed. It is build output, but it is also what GitHub Pages
# serves and the only way to see the map without a fifteen-minute build, so the
# four megabytes are the price of the thing being openable. freesound-raw.json
# is committed for the opposite reason - it is thousands of API requests and the
# one thing here that cannot simply be rebuilt.

*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
